  "limitations": [
    "Steady fps at 1280x720 is \u224813 fps (12.6\u201314.0 measured in 5 live jobs), below the \u226524 fps target; 960x540 reaches 22.5 fps and 640x360 21.6 fps. Raising workers per GPU from 3 to 5 did not help (GPU-bound). First frame 19\u201352 s (\u226460 s target met in all 1280x720 jobs; the 960x540 job hit 72 s while sharing GPUs with another job).",
    "Build scene \u2192 render is sequential: the Cesium scene construction (OnDemand LLM plan + stream) takes 30\u201375 s before the single /api/patch-render POST, so render frames appear ~100\u2013140 s after Build.",
    "Blosm/BlenderGIS add-ons are NOT installed; the pipeline is the in-repo OSM 0.6 + Copernicus DSM + XYZ-ortho importer (terrain.py/geography.py). SRTM/OpenTopography and OSM2World are not used.",
    "MJPEG stream is wired (stream_url) but on these fast 24 fps/5 s jobs the first status poll that sees frames arrives after completion, so the panel showed the latest frame + MP4 rather than the live stream in the recorded runs.",
    "Mockup comparison is quantitative (pixel variance, panel geometry, DOM) \u2014 no side-by-side visual diff tool was available; the Chrome MCP pod was not used for this.",
    "Kane's Boxing Gym placement produced no Vehicles/Debris group (prompt has no crash scenario) \u2014 outliner shows Terrain/Buildings/Roads/Scenery/Camera.",
    "render_service pytest not executed (no pytest on host or in this container); render_service changes validated by syntax check and 11 live jobs.",
